---
import Code from "../../components/Code.astro";
import Docs from "../../layouts/Docs.astro";
---

<Docs
	page="cli"
	title="Command line"
	lede="Every command and flag, what squill prints, and what its exit codes mean."
>
	<section>
		<h2>Commands</h2>
		<Code lang="text" code={`squill [fmt] [OPTIONS] [PATHS...]
squill locate [--json] [OPTIONS] [PATHS...]
squill init [--dialect <D>] [--yaml] [--yes]
squill language-server start
squill help [COMMAND]
squill version`} />
		<ul>
			<li>
				<code>squill fmt</code> formats files, below. It&rsquo;s the default
				command, so <code>squill .</code> formats the working directory,{" "}
				<code>squill -</code> formats stdin, and{" "}
				<code>squill --check .</code> checks. A file named like a command
				needs the <code>fmt</code>, or a path: <code>squill ./init</code>.
			</li>
			<li>
				<code>squill locate</code> lists where the SQL is, <a
					href="docs/cli/#locate">below</a
				>.
			</li>
			<li>
				<code>squill init</code> writes a starter config &mdash; see{" "}
				<a href="docs/configuration/">configuration</a>.
			</li>
			<li>
				<code>squill language-server start</code> serves editors over stdin
				and stdout &mdash; see <a href="docs/editors/">editors</a>.
			</li>
			<li>
				<code>squill help</code> and <code>squill version</code> are{" "}
				<code>--help</code> and <code>--version</code>;{" "}
				<code>squill help locate</code> is <code>squill locate --help</code>.
			</li>
		</ul>
	</section>

	<section>
		<h2>What <code>fmt</code> formats</h2>
		<p>
			Each path is a file or a directory. Directories are searched
			recursively for <code>.sql</code> files, plus whatever the
			config&rsquo;s <a href="docs/configuration/#rules">rules</a> include.
			The search honors <code>.gitignore</code>, skips hidden files, and
			skips the config&rsquo;s <code>ignore</code> globs and any{" "}
			<code>--ignore</code> flags.
		</p>
		<p>
			A file named on the command line is always formatted, ignored or not.
			If no rule covers it, it formats as plain SQL &mdash; unless it is in a
			language squill has a grammar for, in which case squill stops and
			shows the rule to add. <a href="docs/frozen/">Frozen</a> files are the
			exception: they are never rewritten, however they are named.
		</p>
	</section>

	<section>
		<h2>Where the output goes</h2>
		<p>
			By default squill rewrites files in place, listing each one it
			changed. The alternatives:
		</p>
		<div class="scroll">
			<table>
				<thead>
					<tr><th>flag</th><th>does</th></tr>
				</thead>
				<tbody>
					<tr>
						<td><code>--check</code></td>
						<td>
							Writes nothing. Prints a diff for each file that would change,
							and exits 1 if there are any.
						</td>
					</tr>
					<tr>
						<td><code>--stdout</code></td>
						<td>Prints each file&rsquo;s formatted text instead of writing it.</td>
					</tr>
					<tr>
						<td><code>--stdin</code>, <code>-</code></td>
						<td>Reads SQL from stdin and writes it to stdout.</td>
					</tr>
					<tr>
						<td><code>--stdin-filepath &lt;PATH&gt;</code></td>
						<td>
							Reads stdin as the file at <code>PATH</code>, which need not
							exist: its config and rules apply, so a host file&rsquo;s
							embedded SQL formats too. An ignored, frozen, or unconfigured
							host file comes back unchanged. This is the one for editors
							that pipe a buffer through a formatter.
						</td>
					</tr>
				</tbody>
			</table>
		</div>
	</section>

	<section>
		<h2>Options</h2>
		<p>
			The formatting flags &mdash; <code>--dialect</code>,{" "}
			<code>--indent</code>, <code>--indent-width</code>,{" "}
			<code>--max-width</code>, <code>--keyword-case</code>,{" "}
			<code>--quote-idents</code>, <code>--at-params</code>,{" "}
			<code>--question-params</code>, <code>--colon-params</code>, and{" "}
			<code>--pyformat-params</code>{" "}
			&mdash; each set the config key of the same name, and win over the
			config. <a href="docs/configuration/">Configuration</a> lists their
			values.
		</p>
		<div class="scroll">
			<table>
				<thead>
					<tr><th>flag</th><th>does</th></tr>
				</thead>
				<tbody>
					<tr>
						<td><code>--strict</code></td>
						<td>
							Exits 1 when anything was left unformatted: a statement squill
							couldn&rsquo;t parse, or an embedded string it couldn&rsquo;t
							safely rewrite.
						</td>
					</tr>
					<tr>
						<td><code>--locked</code></td>
						<td>
							Fails rather than record a grammar URL that{" "}
							<code>squill.lock</code> doesn&rsquo;t have yet. See{" "}
							<a href="docs/embedded/">embedded SQL</a>.
						</td>
					</tr>
					<tr>
						<td><code>--ignore &lt;GLOB&gt;</code></td>
						<td>
							Skips matching paths while searching directories. Repeatable,
							relative to the working directory, with <code>*</code>,{" "}
							<code>**</code>, <code>?</code>, <code>[abc]</code>, and{" "}
							<code>{"{a,b}"}</code>.
						</td>
					</tr>
					<tr>
						<td><code>--no-config</code></td>
						<td>Ignores config files: built-in defaults and flags only.</td>
					</tr>
					<tr>
						<td><code>--frozen &lt;GLOB&gt;</code></td>
						<td>
							Formats matching files while they&rsquo;re new, and never
							after they exist on the baseline ref. Repeatable. See{" "}
							<a href="docs/frozen/">frozen paths</a>, with{" "}
							<code>--frozen-ref</code> and <code>--no-frozen-fetch</code>.
						</td>
					</tr>
					<tr>
						<td><code>-V</code>, <code>--version</code></td>
						<td>Prints the version.</td>
					</tr>
					<tr>
						<td><code>-h</code>, <code>--help</code></td>
						<td>
							Prints help; <code>squill init --help</code> has its own.
						</td>
					</tr>
				</tbody>
			</table>
		</div>
	</section>

	<section id="locate">
		<h2>Finding the SQL</h2>
		<p>
			<code>squill locate</code> takes the same paths and finds the same
			files as <code>fmt</code>, but formats nothing: it lists every string
			a rule&rsquo;s query captures, whether or not squill would rewrite
			it, and every plain SQL file whole. Each line says where the
			string&rsquo;s contents start and end, which dialect they&rsquo;re
			read in, and how they begin:
		</p>
		<Code lang="text" code={`$ squill locate src/db.rs
src/db.rs:12:9-17:9 postgres  select m.id, m.name…
src/db.rs:24:26-24:68 postgres  SELECT count(*) FROM members`} />
		<p>
			It&rsquo;s the quick way to check a{" "}
			<a href="docs/embedded/#queries">query of your own</a>: a string
			missing from the list is one the query doesn&rsquo;t match. With{" "}
			<code>--json</code>, each line is an object instead &mdash;{" "}
			<code>path</code>, <code>start</code> and <code>end</code> (byte
			offsets), <code>line</code>, <code>column</code>,{" "}
			<code>end_line</code>, <code>end_column</code>,{" "}
			<code>dialect</code>, and <code>pinned_dialect</code> (whether the query set
			the dialect, which the plain output marks{" "}
			<code>(from the query)</code>) &mdash; for tools that want to know where the SQL
			is; these docs highlight the SQL in their recipes with it.
		</p>
	</section>

	<section>
		<h2>Diagnostics</h2>
		<p>
			Whatever squill leaves alone, it says so on stderr, one line each, with
			the place and the reason:
		</p>
		<Code lang="text" code={`queries/report.sql:14:1: expected a statement, found \`frobnicate\` (statement passed through verbatim)
src/db.rs:42:25: embedded SQL did not parse (expected a statement, found \`frobnicate\`); left unformatted`} />
		<p>
			A summary line follows: how many files were checked, how many were (or
			would be) reformatted, and how many diagnostics there were. A
			diagnostic alone doesn&rsquo;t fail the run &mdash; the file is still
			as correct as it was &mdash; unless you pass <code>--strict</code>.
		</p>
	</section>

	<section id="exit-codes">
		<h2>Exit codes</h2>
		<div class="scroll">
			<table>
				<thead>
					<tr><th>code</th><th>means</th></tr>
				</thead>
				<tbody>
					<tr>
						<td><code>0</code></td>
						<td>Done; nothing to report.</td>
					</tr>
					<tr>
						<td><code>1</code></td>
						<td>
							Under <code>--check</code>, a file would change; under{" "}
							<code>--strict</code>, something was left unformatted.
						</td>
					</tr>
					<tr>
						<td><code>2</code></td>
						<td>
							squill couldn&rsquo;t do the job: a bad flag, a broken config, a
							file it couldn&rsquo;t read or write.
						</td>
					</tr>
				</tbody>
			</table>
		</div>
	</section>

	<section>
		<h2>In CI</h2>
		<Code lang="sh" code={`squill fmt --check --strict --locked .`} />
		<p>
			<code>--check</code> fails on anything unformatted, <code>--strict</code>{" "}
			on anything squill couldn&rsquo;t format, and <code>--locked</code> on a
			grammar download nobody has vetted. Drop <code>--strict</code> while
			adopting squill on a tree it doesn&rsquo;t fully understand yet.
		</p>
	</section>
</Docs>
